  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A Face under the default `lift` law does not lift over a hole that is below the cut plane.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs` (Face arm): under `FaceHoles::Lift` it passes the outline of the material at or above the cut plane to the facer.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/material_source.rs`: new `standing_at`. It is `standing_above` read 1 um below the plane.\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/face_holes.rs`: new `beside`. Under `Lift` with an outline, `forbidden` bridges a hole only when that material stands in the hole or within 0.05 mm of it.\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/face.rs`: the doc comment of `face_over` says what `solid` means under `Lift`.\n- A boss in a hole is lifted over as before. A bore whose rim the cut plane reaches is lifted over as before. `CutAir` and `Through` do not change. With no outline, each hole is lifted over as before.\n\n## Cause\n\nA model source gives the facer the silhouette of the whole part. A through-hole in a low flange is a hole of that silhouette. The facer lifted over it also when the cut plane was 5 mm above the rim of the hole.\n\nThe 16 findings of the issue were false. The path did not go below the cut plane. Each convicted move was a row piece beside a lift. Its end stood less than a tool radius from the open outer rim of the region, and verify law (b) reads each region loop as a wall for a law point. With no lift, no row end is near the rim, and the findings stop.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins (red on unchanged upstream main 1ae4d061f, green with the fix):\n\n- `face_holes_below_cut::holes_below_the_cut_plane_are_not_lifted_over` - red before: 8 plunges, expected 1, note `facing rows lifted over the region's holes at the clearance plane`.\n- `face_holes_below_cut::a_face_above_holes_below_the_cut_plane_has_no_gouge_finding` - red before: `Gouge` at moves 2, 11, 14, 37, 40, 49, 52.\n- `face_holes_below_cut::a_hole_whose_rim_the_cut_plane_reaches_is_still_lifted_over` - green before and after. It pins that the old law stays for a hole at the cut plane.\n- `camcraft_motion::machining2d::face_holes::law::lift_bridges_only_the_holes_that_material_at_the_plane_touches` - new unit test.\n\nMutation results:\n\n- Old `generate.rs` from upstream main: the first two app pins are red. Restored: green.\n- Old `face_holes.rs` from upstream main: the first two app pins are red. Restored: green.\n- The `(FaceHoles::Lift, Some(s))` arm removed from `forbidden`: the unit test is red. Restored: green.\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on head 07d10274a is green. 118 steps, 0 failed. The plan had the app and motion lib tests and 116 suites, with `face_holes_below_cut`, `face_holes` and `face_concave_holes`. The run did not use sccache: the sccache server on this machine did not answer compiler calls.\n\nClippy: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The MCP repro of the issue with the real p01-flange part. The pin uses our own flange fixture: a plate with two through-holes beside a boss.\n- A tilted Face (`tilt`), and a Face with area controls (the turned frame). The code path is the one `CutAir` uses for its outline.\n- The release tier and the pixel snapshots.\n- A second defect stays: a lifted row end within a tool radius of the open outer rim is reported as a gouge when the hole is at the cut plane. Issue #2657 has the repro and the cause. This PR does not change that gouge law. The decision file has the reason.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2149 and #1713 change `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`. They change other arms of `run_job_arms`, not the Face arm. The PR that merges second takes a refresh.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/2437-face-holes-below-cut.md`.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Face on a model source no longer lifts over holes that are below the cut plane, and verify no longer reports false gouge findings for them (#2437).\n\nFixes #2437\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
